{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790962302,"nonce":"NuQ1mVd+P+WsYrt2RwNeo41tJlA=","title":"the native backend cannot open a window on Android","message":"winit 0.30 on Android needs one of its activity features (`android-native-activity` or `android-game-activity`) and an `EventLoop` built with the `AndroidApp` that `android_main` receives (`EventLoopBuilder::with_android_app`). native.rs calls `EventLoop::new()`, which panics there (\"An `AndroidApp` as passed to android_main() is required\"), and an adapter checking for aarch64-linux-android fails in android-activity without a feature. CONTRIBUTING.md lists Android among the platforms the backend runs on; it does not yet.\n\nIt needs the host to hand the backend its `AndroidApp` before the first window opens, and the adapter to enable an activity feature.","files":null}]}